Motors, generators, transformers and energy accounts (@em-electromechanics: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @electromagnetism, #source "../sources/Electromagnetic-Fields-and-Energy-Haus-Melcher.lingua#r_1VKHEEC14B3VDGBA13T6K4JQNV", #source "../sources/Electromagnetics-and-Applications-Staelin.lingua#r_45QC1TW6RXJBJE8Q5H98DZT5AC", #electromagnetism "Quasistatic-limits-diffusion-and-skin-depth.lingua#r_7RSC1KG4B4DNB7C7319F691MSW", #electrical-power-engineering "../../../engineering/electrical-power-engineering/machines/Synchronous-machines-power-angle-and-capability.lingua#r_1PBXD8QXNWF5SQBMHCN8CYP8T6") { r_3G4DF28F72Y3GD5QRG19CD75W8
**Read:** [Electromagnetic Fields and Energy — Haus and Melcher](../sources/Electromagnetic-Fields-and-Energy-Haus-Melcher.lingua#r_1VKHEEC14B3VDGBA13T6K4JQNV), complete electromechanical energy and force development; [Electromagnetics and Applications — David H. Staelin](../sources/Electromagnetics-and-Applications-Staelin.lingua#r_45QC1TW6RXJBJE8Q5H98DZT5AC), motors, actuators and transformer applications.

A generator turns mechanical work into electromagnetic energy delivered to a circuit; a motor transfers it in the other direction. The same coupling coefficients appear in a consistent reversible ideal model, while losses and operating constraints set actual performance. A label such as motor or transformer is not a replacement for torque, flux, current and energy equations.

Derive a rotating-loop sinusoidal emf from changing linked flux, then include load current and opposing torque. Track mechanical input, winding heat, magnetic loss and electrical output. For a magnetic actuator, compare energy and coenergy derivatives under fixed flux versus fixed current. The power supply belongs in the account whenever it maintains an imposed current or voltage.

Use these field derivations as interfaces to the distinct power-engineering and machinery subjects. A complete machine also needs magnetic/material characterization, thermal paths, insulation, bearings, control, fabrication, testing and maintenance. Investigate a small isolated teaching apparatus or a fully documented case before extrapolating to industrial equipment. An analytical ideal efficiency is a limit of a model, not an evidence-based claim about a built machine.

**Continue:** [Quasistatic limits, diffusion and skin depth](Quasistatic-limits-diffusion-and-skin-depth.lingua#r_7RSC1KG4B4DNB7C7319F691MSW).

